  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on comparing the minimum probabilities of the lotteries (20% vs. 25%) and choosing the one with the higher minimum probability (Lottery B). However, the individual explicitly states that probabilities are too similar to influence their decision and instead focuses on the higher monetary outcome (4000 Euros). There is no indication that the individual considered the minimum probability of each lottery or used it as a decision rule. On the contrary, they dismiss probability differences as irrelevant. Therefore, the information used by the individual (payoff magnitudes) does not align with the information required by the decision reason (minimum probabilities), and their justification (focus on higher reward) contradicts the rule of the decision reason (prefer higher minimum probability).",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
